gpui_windows: Capture a press for a later drag

`Window::capture_native_drag_gesture` keeps the left-button press being
dispatched, and `NativeDragGesture::claim` later turns it into tracking
authority after the platform checks that the same press is still held by
this window. A release, capture loss, deactivation, a new press or the
window closing invalidates it. Constructed GPUI mouse events cannot
create one.

Newport needs it for Remote apps on Windows: a Linux app starts a drag
after its press has been forwarded, and Newport then starts the outgoing
OLE drag from that press.

capture_native_drag_gesture has a default.

Remove when upstream GPUI can start a native drag from an earlier press.

